BASELINE TRANSFER -- climatology's own coverage, in-sample vs held out
================================================================================================================
  Climatology is the TRAIN block's empirical quantile -- the same 22,683 rows
  every model is fitted on -- so IN-SAMPLE coverage is exact by construction.
  Any gap on the held-out block is REGIME DRIFT in the envelope's level, not a
  modelling choice, and every model below inherits it.
  TRAIN, not train+val: this must use the same block as fit_climatology or the
  diagnostic disagrees with the model it is explaining. It did, briefly --
  0.265 against 0.262 at ALL/MAE/0.5h -- when climatology moved to train and
  this block was left on the fit block.

